- **Top owner:** Vladimir Kochnev is the main source of knowledge. They own `base.rb`, `nesting_exposure.rb`, `nested_exposures.rb`, `represent_exposure.rb`, `formatter_exposure.rb` and 3 more files. They have no commit since 2015, so they can't be asked.
- **Practical reviewer:** Marco Silva is the most active owner of the directory. They own `grouped_exposure.rb` outright (117 lines, 100%). The tool lists those lines as "placeholder identities" (`<email redacted>`). The same person also appears under `marco.silva@kestrel.example`, a strong match. Both of those are guesses from names and addresses, and I haven't merged or confirmed them.
- **Second active person:** Anna Kowalczyk is active but holds only 4 lines (0.7%).
- **Files with a single author:** `grouped_exposure.rb` (Marco Silva), `represent_exposure.rb`, `formatter_exposure.rb`, `block_exposure.rb` and `formatter_block_exposure.rb` (all Kochnev). Alexander Yunin owns `nesting_exposure/output_builder.rb` (59 lines, 86.4%).

## Delegator code
The delegator code is `lib/grape_entity/delegator.rb` plus `lib/grape_entity/delegators/`. There is also `exposure/delegator_exposure.rb`, which falls under the directory above.

- **`delegators/`** has 61 non-blank lines (69 counting blank lines). Vladimir Kochnev holds 47 (77.0%) and 50 (72.5%). Paul Padier holds 5 (8.2%) and James McCarthy 4 (6.6%). None of the 5 authors has committed in the last year, so all 4 files are orphaned.
- **`delegator.rb`** has 24 non-blank lines (27 counting blank lines). Vladimir Kochnev holds 11 (45.8%) and 12 (44.4%). Paul Padier holds 6 (25.0%). Marco Silva holds 4 (16.7%) and is the only active author, with a commit on 2026-07-21.
- **Reviewer:** Marco Silva for `delegator.rb`, with only 4 lines of experience there. Nobody active has written `delegators/`, so any reviewer there is a stand-in. Paul Padier (last commit 2021-10-15) is the closest person to ask about it.

## Who has effectively left
- **Directory `exposure/`:** Vladimir Kochnev, Alexander Yunin, James McCarthy and Dmitry Tsepelev have no commit in the last 365 days. Of the 18 authors, 2 are active and hold 19.9% of the lines. 80.1% of the lines belong to people with no recent commit, and 9 files (80.8% of the lines) are orphaned.
- **Directory `delegators/`:** 0 of 5 authors are active, so 100% of its lines are orphaned.
- **Whole repository:** 7 of 87 people committed in the last year and hold 10.7% of the non-blank lines. Vladimir Kochnev's last commit anywhere was 2015-09-18, so they have left the project, not just the path. The bus factor for `exposure/` is 1 on both bases (Kochnev alone holds 54.4% of 609 non-blank lines and 54.6% of 732 counting blank lines). Reaching 80% takes 3 authors.

## Does the person with the most commits own the most code?
